{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Basil","id":"339235123759153162","is_bot":0,"username":"divinedefault"},"author_id":"339235123759153162","channel_id":"746939355003748354","content":"mk, i forgot about our conversations about PC death concepts this year. so i think now that i'm understanding the lines of communication (community->mods/dm's->discussion->dm decision) the poll wouldn't be as nescessary so long as the mods also help quell people's concerns as to why we decide on these types of rules.\n\nso with rule philosophy taken care of, i think players rolling is the best way to go because we do have a semi-large playerbase with anxiety. so simply because we can't guarantee how people would react not knowing what happens behind the curtain we should keep it to the channel and dying role. (this is my two-cents, i can't speak for the other mods and dms)","created_at":"2021-03-23T03:46:59.883000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"823764744439332906","reply_to_id":"823760786354077707","thread":null,"thread_id":null}
